UNODC is currently negotiating an UN-to-UN agreement with UNDP to implement a component on trafficking in persons of their CARISECURE 2.0 Project (in Antigua and Barbuda, Barbados, Saint Lucia and Trinidad and Tobago), that encompasses:
•	Development and implementation of a regional standardized Law Enforcement Counter Trafficking in Persons (TIP) Toolkit (LECTT);
•	Training on the LECTT and training for Barbados’ Sex Crimes and Trafficking Unit and Immigration Officers on TIP SOPs

UNCTAD's Automated System for Customs Data (ASYCUDA) is an integrated customs management system for international trade and transport operations, providing technical assistance and capacity building for comprehensive Customs modernization.

Through the ASYCUDA programme, UNCTAD to:
Modernizing customs operations and helping to improve revenue collection;
Facilitating trade efficiency and competitiveness by substantially reducing transaction time and costs;
Improving security by streamlining procedures of cargo control, transit of goods and clearance of goods;
Helping fight corruption by enhancing the transparency of transactions;
Promoting sustainable development by cutting down on the use of paper, through the use of electronic transactions and documents

The iCOAST programme aims to drive change in the tourism sector by creating an enabling policy and regulatory environment – supported by financial mechanisms and products (1) that supports and incentivizes governments, private sector and local communities to introduce and benefit from sustainable tourism practices, (2) drives the development of local sustainable supply chains, and (3) makes it convenient for tourists to make sustainable choices.

There are 4 programme components: Policy and Regulations; Finance and Investment; Technical Assistance and Introduction of Alternative Practices, Technologies and Business Models; and Global Coordination and Knowledge Dissemination;

The programme approach addresses the following:
Environmental sustainability – plastic pollution, food waste, energy savings, water and waste management innovation;
Social sustainability – community engagement, capacity building job creation, entrepreneurship;
Economic sustainability – supporting local suppliers, fair trade practices and procurement, sustainable investments;
Enhancing resilience – conservation of cultural and natural heritage, benefit sharing of tourism, better positioning of destination.

